{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-03T09:59:26.362Z","author":"pi-toolchain-glm-1103","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"glm-5.3:cloud","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"9e1c18dd119f0404d66458ad","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"glm-5.3:cloud","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-03T09:59:26.362Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-11-03T09:59:26.357Z","author":"pi-toolchain-glm-1103","text":"Reproduced both failures locally: test/batch-triage.test.ts 'deleted and missing source documents...' expects jev_triage_failure for the missing-file case and test/link.test.ts 'link backlog preserves missing-source host failures...' expects jev_link_failure; both rows now report the host code item_not_found. Root cause: pm-cli 2026.10.28 GH-1613 preserves typed PmClient lookup refusals, so a missing item document surfaces item_not_found through the pm-jev error mapping instead of falling back to the generic decision-failure codes. Classification: test pinned old CLI behaviour; production code is correct (the host error is retained, receipts are not applied, exit code stays 1). Fix: assert item_not_found for the missing-document cases and document the upstream reference in a comment; keep every other assertion."}]}],"before_hash":"1817a707ba338ee3cc8fe597c4539cc52ad04f84b0a499f56c491c55c005f275","after_hash":"0f5d6d87d222c452f9bacfd7e254b66ba229f0b39b22220a2b7a82fbb555d4bf","item_hash_version":3,"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"80136dd0c3b60addc8b612a62bb28f570f4dbd4db83f5f05a1f87ab469a48965"}
